From d02e4ae1d80e00ef84e394104adb221459085ec7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: testuser <mainta@example.test>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 05:27:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] fix(cli): report the turn's token usage in the ACP
 session/prompt result

Under ACP, prompt() returned only `stopReason`: the run result's usage and the
core's usage events were dropped, so an ACP client could not meter a Cline
session (upstream cli-v3.0.65 answers every session/prompt with no usage).

prompt() now reads the session's accumulated usage (primary agent plus spawned
agents) before and after the turn and returns the difference as ACP
`PromptResponse.usage`. Core input totals include cache reads and writes, so
`inputTokens` is the uncached remainder, `cachedReadTokens` and
`cachedWriteTokens` are reported apart, and `totalTokens` is the sum of the
four. Without a core usage summary the run result's usage is reported; with
none the result has no `usage` field. The usage baseline is read before the
post-initialization abort check, so a cancel that lands while it is read still
cancels the turn before send().
